invariant: INV-17
file: src/chacha20_avx512.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: pass_with_rows loses its noinline, so the pinned clang inlines it
  into chacha20_avx512_xor. Its reads of the input words then let clang
  keep the key the entry loaded in a register across the calls of pass,
  and clang 23 saved a copy of that register in the entry's frame, which
  no wipe names. Every byte the kernel writes is still right. The script
  compiles the kernel for x86-64 and requires chacha20_avx512_xor to call
  pass_with_rows.

--- old
static __attribute__((noinline)) void pass_with_rows(const uint32_t words[16], uint32_t counter,
--- new
static void pass_with_rows(const uint32_t words[16], uint32_t counter,
